  continuous (thickness/intensity/hue) tolerance = that attribute's own CNN predictor's
  test-set MAE, **floored at 5% of the p15-p85 gap**. The floor was needed after a real
  bug surfaced in testing: hue's predictor is so accurate (MAE~0.0007 on a [0,1] scale)
  that using its raw MAE as tolerance made success require landing within a fraction of a
  percent of the target — CC came back exactly 0.0 for both hue directions before the fix,
  not because the model failed but because the bar was unreachable by construction.
